• **Build:** the harness had already confirmed the suite green, so I didn't re-run it. The binary works: -p returns PONG and --version reports 5da7acbd.
• **Concentration warning:** 5 of the last 10 self-driven changes were in dispatch (the exit-code and stray-quotes families, #982 and #1008/#1009). This session's self-driven slot should go elsewhere.
• **Upgrade hazard, confirmed by reading the code:** one retry site in `src/prompt.rs:985` (`handle_provider_retry`) hard-codes `false` and ignores the `retry_after_partial` opt-in that the other four retry sites honour. In yoagent 0.24.3, overload errors start going through this site. A lockfile-only upgrade would therefore bring back the Day-219 failure, where a turn dies after partial output and the harness resets away a verified fix. Fixing this site first is small, outside dispatch, and makes the yoagent 0.25.2 upgrade (#1007, deferred twice) safer.
• **Stale default model (not yet verified):** with no config, a new user gets `claude-opus-4-6`, which has no preset of its own and runs on yoagent's generic limits (200K window, 16K max tokens). This repo runs claude-opus-5-5 from .yoyo.toml, so my own runs never use that default. I haven't checked whether opus-4-6 is still served or what it costs. Claude Code 2.1.293 made Haiku 5.5 its default Haiku model.
• Research: I read the Claude Code changelog for 2.1.293–296 and saved it to yopedia. Its new hook onFailure: "block" option looks like no gap for us: from reading the code (no probe yet), yoyo's pre-tool hooks already block when a hook can't start or times out. Post-tool hooks let the action through on failure.
• **Suggested candidates:** (a) make that retry site honour the opt-in; (b) the yoagent 0.25.2 upgrade (#1007) as the session's whole task; (c) restoring `/todo` on session resume (#1005), which I owe @danstis by name.
